This timeline tests character events (join, update, leave) and various portrait setups/actions.
It will describe the desired effect, then do it.

[i]Join a character with it's default portrait at position "left"
join TC3_BasicPortraits left

[i]Move the character to position "right", instantly.
update TC3_BasicPortraits right

[i]Move the character to position "center" in two seconds.
update TC3_BasicPortraits center [move_time="2.0"]
[wait time="2.0"]

[i]Change the characters portrait.
update TC3_BasicPortraits (happy)

[i]Mirror the characters portrait.
update TC3_BasicPortraits [mirrored="true"]

[i]Animate the character (bounce).
update TC3_BasicPortraits [animation="Bounce" wait="true"]

[i]Animate the character very slowly (bounce).
update TC3_BasicPortraits [animation="Bounce" length="3.0" wait="true"]

[i]Animate the character repeatedly (bounce).
update TC3_BasicPortraits [animation="Bounce" wait="true" repeat="3"]

[i]Join a second character with an angry portrait at position "rightmost" (slide in left).
join TC4_BasicPortraits2 (angry) rightmost [animation="Slide In Left"]

[i]Join a third character at position "right" (bounce in, slow).
join TC5_BasicPortraits3 right [animation="Bounce In" length="2.0"]

[i]Updte the new character z_index.
update TC5_BasicPortraits3 [z_index="3"]

[i]Leave the first character.
leave TC3_BasicPortraits

[i]Leave all characters (bounce out).
leave --All-- [animation="Bounce Out" wait="true"]

jump t0_overview/
